From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Andres Cera <andres.cera@hotmail.com>
Date: Mon, 10 Aug 2026 18:00:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 19/26] media: rockchip: rkvenc: fix the worker's lock context and the dma-buf import API

MOTIVATION. A plain, unfaulted 1080p encode on a Rock 5B+ running
a KASAN+LOCKDEP kernel produced three reports, all from 0001's
imported driver and none of them from fault injection:

  BUG: sleeping function called from invalid context at
  kernel/locking/mutex.c:623 ... name: rkvenc-worker
  1 lock held by rkvenc-worker/249:
   #0: (&queue->running_lock){....}-{3:3}, at:
   rkvenc_task_worker_default+0x108
  [ BUG: Invalid wait context ] trying to lock
   (&queue->pending_lock){+.+.}-{4:4}, at:
   rkvenc_task_worker_default+0x1d4
  WARNING: drivers/dma-buf/dma-buf.c:1179 at
  dma_buf_map_attachment+0x184, rkvenc_dma_import_fd

Two independent defects. First, rkvenc_task_worker_default() takes
queue->running_lock with spin_lock_irqsave() and then, still
holding it with interrupts off, takes queue->pending_lock -- which
0001 declares as a struct mutex. That is a sleeping lock acquired
from atomic context; it can schedule with interrupts disabled and
deadlock the box, and lockdep flags the {3:3}-inside-{4:4} wait
context before it gets that far. Second, rkvenc_dma_import_fd()
and rkvenc_dma_release_buffer() call the LOCKED dma-buf entry
points, dma_buf_map_attachment() and dma_buf_unmap_attachment(),
which since the dynamic-importer split assert the caller holds the
exporter's reservation lock. rkvenc holds no such lock and is not
a dynamic importer, so every single buffer import trips
dma_resv_assert_held(). The two are unrelated: the WARNING fires
in ioctl context on a task that never touches either queue lock.

BEHAVIOUR. pending_lock becomes a spinlock_t, initialised with
spin_lock_init() and taken with spin_lock()/spin_unlock() at both
of its two sites. running_lock deliberately stays held across the
dequeue: claiming an idle core and taking the task that will
occupy it has to be one step, or two workers on different cores
can claim the same core_id. Neither pending_lock critical section
sleeps or is anything but an O(1) list operation, so the type
change costs nothing and is what the nesting already required.
The dma-buf calls move to dma_buf_map_attachment_unlocked() and
dma_buf_unmap_attachment_unlocked(), the entry points for static
importers that do not hold dmabuf->resv, which is exactly what
this driver is: it attaches with plain dma_buf_attach() and
registers no dma_buf_attach_ops.

NON-GOALS. No lockdep suppression, no lockdep_off(), no
might_sleep() annotation change -- the lock order is fixed, not
hidden. The worker is not restructured and no work item is added:
the dequeue does not need to move contexts once the lock it takes
is the right type. No new locking is introduced and no critical
section grows.

PROVENANCE. First-party CeraLive fix to the imported 0001 driver.
Both defects are 0001's as imported -- neither the 0013 test hook
nor the 0014 teardown work touches this block, and 0014's
pending_lock edits are all on the unrelated session->pending_lock.
No upstream counterpart: the VEPU580 driver is not in mainline.

EVIDENCE POINTER. Root-caused from a REAL Rock 5B+ KASAN+LOCKDEP
boot log, not a self-test: the splat names both locks, both
acquisition offsets in rkvenc_task_worker_default, and the exact
dma-buf line. Source-verified against v7.1.7's own
drivers/dma-buf/dma-buf.c, where line 1179 is
dma_resv_assert_held(attach->dmabuf->resv). Build-clean; the
runtime re-test on the debug slot is the confirming evidence and
is pending. See docs/BOARD-QUALIFICATION.md.

First-party: authored by CeraLive against v7.1.7, with no upstream
counterpart in rockchip-rk3588-mainline-patches. The source of record is
ceralive/0019-rkvenc-worker-lock-context-and-dma-buf-api.patch; patches/ is generated from it by
scripts/build-series.py, and scripts/verify-payload-parity.py holds it to the
same added/removed-line parity the upstream lane gets.

NOT upstream-bound: this targets the CeraLive device tree only and is not a
submission to linux-media, linux-rockchip or the fork parent. No Signed-off-by
is added, because a DCO assertion belongs to whoever actually submits it.

---
diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/rockchip/rkvenc/rkvenc_hw.h b/drivers/media/platform/rockchip/rkvenc/rkvenc_hw.h
--- a/drivers/media/platform/rockchip/rkvenc/rkvenc_hw.h
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/rockchip/rkvenc/rkvenc_hw.h
@@ -371,7 +371,15 @@ struct rkvenc_iommu_info {
 /* ---- Task queue ---- */
 struct rkvenc_taskqueue {
 	struct mutex session_lock;
-	struct mutex pending_lock;
+	/*
+	 * pending_lock nests INSIDE running_lock: the worker claims an idle
+	 * core and dequeues the task it will run as one atomic step, so the
+	 * dequeue happens with running_lock held and interrupts off. A
+	 * sleeping lock cannot be acquired there. Both of pending_lock's
+	 * critical sections are O(1) list operations that never sleep, so a
+	 * spinlock costs nothing and is the type the nesting requires.
+	 */
+	spinlock_t pending_lock;
 	spinlock_t running_lock;
 	struct mutex dev_lock;
 
diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/rockchip/rkvenc/rkvenc_iommu.c b/drivers/media/platform/rockchip/rkvenc/rkvenc_iommu.c
--- a/drivers/media/platform/rockchip/rkvenc/rkvenc_iommu.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/rockchip/rkvenc/rkvenc_iommu.c
@@ -63,7 +63,16 @@ static void rkvenc_dma_release_buffer(struct kref *ref)
 	buffer->dma->buffer_count--;
 	list_move_tail(&buffer->link, &buffer->dma->unused_list);
 
-	dma_buf_unmap_attachment(buffer->attach, buffer->sgt, buffer->dir);
+	/*
+	 * The _unlocked variant is the one for importers that do NOT hold the
+	 * exporter's reservation lock, which is this driver: it attaches with
+	 * plain dma_buf_attach() and registers no dma_buf_attach_ops, so it is
+	 * a static importer and never takes dmabuf->resv itself. The locked
+	 * entry point asserts that lock is held and trips
+	 * dma_resv_assert_held() when it is not.
+	 */
+	dma_buf_unmap_attachment_unlocked(buffer->attach, buffer->sgt,
+					  buffer->dir);
 	dma_buf_detach(buffer->dmabuf, buffer->attach);
 	dma_buf_put(buffer->dmabuf);
 	buffer->dma = NULL;
@@ -177,10 +186,11 @@ rkvenc_dma_import_fd(struct rkvenc_iommu_info *iommu_info,
 		goto fail_attach;
 	}
 
-	sgt = dma_buf_map_attachment(attach, buffer->dir);
+	sgt = dma_buf_map_attachment_unlocked(attach, buffer->dir);
 	if (IS_ERR(sgt)) {
 		ret = PTR_ERR(sgt);
-		rkvenc_err("dma_buf_map_attachment fd %d failed(%d)\n", fd, ret);
+		rkvenc_err("dma_buf_map_attachment_unlocked fd %d failed(%d)\n",
+			   fd, ret);
 		goto fail_map;
 	}
 	buffer->iova = sg_dma_address(sgt->sgl);
diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/rockchip/rkvenc/rkvenc_service.c b/drivers/media/platform/rockchip/rkvenc/rkvenc_service.c
--- a/drivers/media/platform/rockchip/rkvenc/rkvenc_service.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/rockchip/rkvenc/rkvenc_service.c
@@ -821,7 +821,16 @@ void rkvenc_task_worker_default(struct kthread_work *work)
 		core_id = find_first_bit(&core_idle, queue->core_id_max + 1);
 
 		if (core_id <= queue->core_id_max && queue->cores[core_id]) {
-			mutex_lock(&queue->pending_lock);
+			/*
+			 * running_lock stays held across the dequeue on
+			 * purpose: finding an idle core and taking the task
+			 * that will occupy it must be one step, or two
+			 * workers racing on different cores can both claim
+			 * the same core_id. That is why pending_lock is a
+			 * spinlock -- this acquisition happens with
+			 * interrupts already disabled.
+			 */
+			spin_lock(&queue->pending_lock);
 			pending_task = list_first_entry_or_null(&queue->pending_list,
 								struct rkvenc_mpp_task,
 								queue_link);
@@ -831,7 +840,7 @@ void rkvenc_task_worker_default(struct kthread_work *work)
 				pending_task->mpp = queue->cores[core_id];
 				pending_task->core_id = core_id;
 			}
-			mutex_unlock(&queue->pending_lock);
+			spin_unlock(&queue->pending_lock);
 		}
 		spin_unlock_irqrestore(&queue->running_lock, flags);
 
@@ -1207,9 +1216,9 @@ static long rkvenc_dev_ioctl(struct file *filp, unsigned int cmd, unsigned long
 
 		/* Add to task queue and trigger worker */
 		set_bit(TASK_STATE_PENDING, &task->mpp_task.state);
-		mutex_lock(&queue->pending_lock);
+		spin_lock(&queue->pending_lock);
 		list_add_tail(&task->mpp_task.queue_link, &queue->pending_list);
-		mutex_unlock(&queue->pending_lock);
+		spin_unlock(&queue->pending_lock);
 
 		/* Trigger the worker to run the task */
 		kthread_queue_work(&queue->worker, &session->mpp->work);
@@ -1403,7 +1412,7 @@ int rkvenc_service_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 			return -ENOMEM;
 
 		mutex_init(&queue->session_lock);
-		mutex_init(&queue->pending_lock);
+		spin_lock_init(&queue->pending_lock);
 		spin_lock_init(&queue->running_lock);
 		mutex_init(&queue->dev_lock);
 		INIT_LIST_HEAD(&queue->session_attach);
